<%# The User view — the dashboard's decision board.

    ONE list, not two. The Ranked view splits priority above spot because the two
    halves answer different questions there; this view deliberately does not,
    because it is the screen you scroll top to bottom clicking Trash, Trash,
    Trash. The split survives only as the ordering (every priority row sorts above
    every spot row) and as a badge on each row.

    What "reorder" means here is the session's `precedence`, the same integer the
    spot queue is actually started in — so dragging a row is a real scheduling
    decision, not a display preference. That is stated in the hint below rather
    than left to be discovered.

    NO PAGINATOR, on purpose, for the same reason the Ranked view has none: a drag
    between two rows means nothing if one of them is on another page. The list is
    capped instead, and says so when it has truncated.

    Locals:
      sessions          - the ordered rows (priority above spot, precedence within)
      limit             - the cap the list was rendered under
      truncated         - whether the cap was reached
      visibility_filter - which board this is; the shared visibility controller
                          reads it to decide whether a snoozed row leaves the DOM %>
<section class="mb-8"
         id="user_view"
         data-controller="user-view"
         data-user-view-reorder-url-template-value="<%= reorder_precedence_session_path("__ID__") %>">
  <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Your board</h2>
      <p class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-gray-500">
        Every session these filters match, in the order it will be worked. Decide on the row:
        merge a green PR, snooze it, or trash it. Drag a row to move it — that writes its
        <span class="font-medium text-gray-600">precedence</span>, which is the order Zimmer
        actually starts spot sessions in. Priority rows always sort above spot ones.
      </p>
    </div>
    <%= render "sessions/user_view_reprioritize", reprioritizer_session: nil %>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
    <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gray-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-gray-600"
          data-user-view-target="count"><%= sessions.size %></span>
    <span class="min-w-0 text-xs text-gray-400">rows on this board</span>
  </div>

  <%# The list is always in the DOM, hidden when empty: it is the Sortable root and
      a target that disappears when the board empties would take drag-and-drop down
      with it — and it is where a restored row is prepended. %>
  <ul id="user_view_list"
      class="divide-y divide-gray-100 rounded-md border border-gray-200 bg-white <%= "hidden" if sessions.empty? %>"
      data-user-view-target="list">
    <% sessions.each do |session| %>
      <%= render "sessions/user_view_row", agent_session: session %>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <p class="rounded-md border border-dashed border-gray-200 px-3 py-4 text-sm text-gray-400 <%= "hidden" if sessions.any? %>"
     data-user-view-target="empty">No sessions match these filters.</p>

  <% if truncated %>
    <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">Showing the first <%= limit %>. Narrow the filters to see the rest.</p>
  <% end %>

  <%# One live region for the whole board, so a failed reorder says so rather than
      a page reload silently swallowing the drag that just happened. %>
  <p class="mt-3 hidden text-sm text-red-600" role="alert" data-user-view-target="error"></p>
</section>
